From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:53:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] AROS: say that a configured formatter was not run

Helix cannot start programs on AROS: helix_stdx::process refuses each
one before anything is started. A formatter set in languages.toml then
failed with "Failed to spawn formatter <path>: Unsupported", which does
not tell the user why. On AROS, :format now says that the formatter was
not run because starting programs is not supported yet. Other errors and
other platforms are unchanged.

Saving with auto-format still writes the file unformatted and logs the
reason, as Helix does when a formatter fails.
---
 helix-view/src/document.rs | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/helix-view/src/document.rs b/helix-view/src/document.rs
index 2b44c96eb28a2c935f16ed250aa1aa96cae3e8dc..8fdc5253420701f3902a1e76bb315d0c9a42fc0e 100644
--- a/helix-view/src/document.rs
+++ b/helix-view/src/document.rs
@@ -2306,6 +2306,15 @@ impl std::error::Error for FormatterError {}
 impl Display for FormatterError {
     fn fmt(&self, f: &mut std::fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> std::fmt::Result {
         match self {
+            // AROS: helix_stdx::process refuses every program before starting it.
+            #[cfg(target_os = "aros")]
+            Self::SpawningFailed { command, error } if *error == std::io::ErrorKind::Unsupported => {
+                write!(
+                    f,
+                    "Formatter {} was not run: starting programs from Helix is not supported on AROS yet",
+                    command
+                )
+            }
             Self::SpawningFailed { command, error } => {
                 write!(f, "Failed to spawn formatter {}: {:?}", command, error)
             }
